/-!
# Lane `sk-leavitt-06`: abstract ordered 2-complexes (aggregate module)

Purely combinatorial definitions behind Brown's presentation in Khanh (arXiv:2609.08428v1),
proof of Theorem 5.1, tex l.452–460.  Tex l.460: "Homotopies of edge paths are generated by
backtracking and passages across individual triangles. ... In particular, the two ordered edge
cells $(u,v)$ and $(v,u)$ remain distinct."

Namespace `GroupApproximation.Manuscript.SimpleKazhdanSofic.LeavittK2`.

* `TwoComplex.Basic`: `OrderedTwoComplex` (`edge`, `tri`, `tri_edge01/12/02`),
  `OrderedTwoComplex.EdgePath` (`nil`, `fwd`, `bwd`), `Connected`, `EdgePath.append`,
  `EdgePath.reverse` with `append_assoc`, `append_nil`, `reverse_append`, `reverse_reverse`.
* `TwoComplex.Homotopy`: `EdgePath.Move` (backtracking and one triangle passage in context),
  `EdgePath.Homotopic := Relation.EqvGen Move`, congruence (`Homotopic.congr_append`,
  `congr_fwd`, `congr_bwd`), the basic moves as homotopies, `OrderedTwoComplex.SimplyConnected`.
* `TwoComplex.Reverse`: `Homotopic.congr_reverse`, `append_reverse_self`, `reverse_append_self`,
  `SimplyConnected.homotopic` (any two paths with the same endpoints are homotopic).
* `TwoComplex.Action`: `OrderedTwoComplex.Action X G` (a `MulAction G V` preserving ordered
  edges and triangles), `EdgePath.translate`, `translate_append`, `translate_reverse`,
  `Homotopic.translate`.

No topology is used; `T² = 1` and the other derived relations are left to the Brown lanes.
-/
